<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Flow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <apiVersion>63.0</apiVersion>
    <areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>false</areMetricsLoggedToDataCloud>
    <customErrors>
        <description>Displaying Error Message</description>
        <name>GSC_Cannot_edit_Resolved_Case_Error</name>
        <label>Cannot edit &apos;Resolved&apos; Case Error</label>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>539</locationY>
        <customErrorMessages>
            <errorMessage>You cannot edit a resolved case. If you need to make changes, please reopen the case and proceed with the edits.</errorMessage>
            <isFieldError>false</isFieldError>
        </customErrorMessages>
    </customErrors>
    <decisions>
        <description>This decision is used for checking the Record types for Case object. 
Kindly utilise this flow for all the after create/update case validations.</description>
        <name>Check_Record_Type</name>
        <label>Check Record Type</label>
        <locationX>380</locationX>
        <locationY>323</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>GSC_Is_Global_Service_case</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.RecordType.DeveloperName</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Global_Service_Case</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>GSC_Custom_Validation_Check</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Is Global Service case</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <decisions>
        <description>This decision is checking the criteria for case validation errors for record type &quot;Global Service Case&quot;.
1 - Cannot edit &apos;Resolved&apos; Case: This criteria is checking the Custom Permission &quot;Allow_Edit_on_Resolved_Global_Service_Cases&quot; is FALSE that means other than admins no one is allowed to edit the Resolved Global Service Cases. For reference, check user story #29276 on Gitlab
Added Follow Up Required logic to bypass Follow Up Required Field Update on Case as per Gitlab #31866</description>
        <name>GSC_Custom_Validation_Check</name>
        <label>GSC Custom Validation Check</label>
        <locationX>182</locationX>
        <locationY>431</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Default Outcome</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>GSC_Cannot_edit_Resolved_Case</name>
            <conditionLogic>((1 AND 2) OR (3 AND 4)) AND 5 AND 6</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Resolved</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record__Prior.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Resolved</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>NotEqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Reopened</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record__Prior.Status</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <stringValue>Resolved</stringValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Permission.Allow_Edit_on_Resolved_Global_Service_Cases</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>$Record.Follow_Up_Required__c</leftValueReference>
                <operator>IsChanged</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>false</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>GSC_Cannot_edit_Resolved_Case_Error</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>1 - Cannot edit &apos;Resolved&apos; Case</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>This flow handles the custom validations error for all the record types in Case After Create &amp; Update Scenarios. For reference, check user story #29276 on Gitlab
Note: This flow should be kept at last in the Order of Flow Execution as it will fail other After create/update flows.</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <interviewLabel>Case Custom Validation {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Case - Custom Validations Flow</label>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>BuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>CanvasMode</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>AUTO_LAYOUT_CANVAS</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processMetadataValues>
        <name>OriginBuilderType</name>
        <value>
            <stringValue>LightningFlowBuilder</stringValue>
        </value>
    </processMetadataValues>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <start>
        <locationX>254</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Check_Record_Type</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterFormula>{!$Record.RecordType.DeveloperName} = &apos;Global_Service_Case&apos;</filterFormula>
        <object>Case</object>
        <recordTriggerType>CreateAndUpdate</recordTriggerType>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
    <triggerOrder>1500</triggerOrder>
</Flow>
